        {"h2_html": "What Thryv <em>does well</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Thryv is a capable, well-established platform, and it earns its place in this comparison. It pulls a broad set of tools into one login: a CRM, online scheduling, invoicing and payments, listings across many directories, reputation and review tools, and email and SMS marketing, all in one connected system. On its own site Thryv also describes managed marketing services you can add on, plus live support for the people using it. If what you want is a single subscription that replaces a stack of separate apps, that breadth is a genuine strength.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">The part worth understanding is the model. Thryv is a platform you and your staff log into and operate. You manage the CRM, you build the campaigns, you keep the calendar current, and the managed services sit as add-ons around that core. For an owner who wants to be hands-on and stay in the driver seat, that control is the whole appeal. The only real question is whether running the software is work you want to own, or work you would rather hand off.</p>'},
